From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 05:11:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] prntvpt, wineps.drv: offer the driver's two-sided printing to
 Word.

Word lists "Print on both sides" from the printer's Print Schema, not from
DeviceCapabilities, and only while every step of its PrintTicket round trip
works.  prntvpt now describes the job duplex feature -- one-sided, long and
short edge, constrained to nothing -- in the capabilities and carries it both
ways between tickets and DEVMODEs, and fills in the capability features that
were stubs, with display names Word shows.

PTConvertPrintTicketToDevMode() returns the driver's whole DEVMODE, private
part included, as Windows does: Office compares its size with the DEVMODE it
passed in and gives up on the printer when they differ.  A paper given by its
size alone -- dmPaperSize 0 with the width and length set, which is how Word
passes the page of the document -- is recognised or kept as a size instead of
failing the conversion.  The paper width and length flags were swapped.

wineps names the choices the way Windows and HP's driver do, flip on the
long or short edge, and says it can collate, since the job ticket carries it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5a15eab8621b8f800e2dd81cf918848cb912fda5)

